A. The constant from the discs: every cloud of a million points or more, the three estimates
   a_tot   by size: 1.32604, 1.32592, 1.32599, 1.32600, 1.32592; weighted mean 1.32596, standard error 0.00001; 4/3 is 551 standard errors above
   a_prof  by size: 1.32596, 1.32596, 1.32599, 1.32596, 1.32592; weighted mean 1.32595, standard error 0.00002; 4/3 is 457 standard errors above
   a_size  by size: 1.32595, 1.32586, 1.32594, 1.32596, 1.32592; weighted mean 1.32592, standard error 0.00001; 4/3 is 736 standard errors above
   the three estimates rest on the same clouds, so they are not three witnesses; the cell problem (B) is another
   are the sizes alike? a_tot at 10^6, 3x10^6, 10^7, 3x10^7, 10^8 against their weighted mean: chi-square 10.7 on 4 degrees of freedom
