F. Grid points, vertices only. Rote, Rueber and Saghafian (2024) proved the grid's constant, (pi^2 / (2 zeta(3)))^(1/3) = 1.60121, for parabolas
   grid points in a disc of radius  100 (31417 points): 541 layers; divided by (3/4) radius^(4/3): 1.5541 (the grid constant, if the flow holds for a disc: 1.6012)
   grid points in a disc of radius  200 (125629 points): 1365 layers; divided by (3/4) radius^(4/3): 1.5561 (the grid constant, if the flow holds for a disc: 1.6012)
   grid points in a disc of radius  400 (502625 points): 3464 layers; divided by (3/4) radius^(4/3): 1.5671 (the grid constant, if the flow holds for a disc: 1.6012)
   grid points in a disc of radius  800 (2010573 points): 8763 layers; divided by (3/4) radius^(4/3): 1.5733 (the grid constant, if the flow holds for a disc: 1.6012)
   the  250 x  250 grid: 918 layers; divided by the constant and side^(4/3): 0.3640; over the same for a disc of area 1, 0.3496: 1.0411
   the  500 x  500 grid: 2302 layers; divided by the constant and side^(4/3): 0.3623; over the same for a disc of area 1, 0.3496: 1.0361
   the 1000 x 1000 grid: 5836 layers; divided by the constant and side^(4/3): 0.3645; over the same for a disc of area 1, 0.3496: 1.0424
   the 2000 x 2000 grid: 14709 layers; divided by the constant and side^(4/3): 0.3646; over the same for a disc of area 1, 0.3496: 1.0426
   (the last column should tend to what random points give for a square against a disc, in E, if both follow the same flow)

